# Normalize every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` checks the tree
# out as CRLF while the blobs stay LF. Any tool that then rewrites a file with
# LF — a formatter, a bundler — leaves the on-disk size disagreeing with the
# size Git cached at checkout, and every such file shows as modified with an
# empty diff. Pinning eol here keeps the setting with the repository instead of
# relying on each contributor's local config.
#
# There are no .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files in this tree; add an `eol=crlf` rule below
# if one is ever introduced, since those require CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets. `text=auto` already detects these, but naming them keeps a
# mis-detected file from being line-ending mangled.
*.png   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.ttf   binary
